From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pip_package: add riscv64 to the wheel platform table

Upstream-Status: To upstream [no riscv64 CI runner upstream yet]

BDistWheel.get_tag() in pip_package/setup.py maps platform.machine() to a
wheel platform tag by hand, with a bare `assert machine == "x86_64"` as the
fallback. On riscv64 that assertion fails before a wheel can even be named,
regardless of whether the prebuilt vgfpy extension itself built cleanly.

manylinux_2_39_riscv64 is the flavour of the image these wheels are built in
(quay.io/pypa/manylinux_2_39_riscv64, Rocky Linux 10, glibc 2.39); the x86_64
and aarch64 branches keep their own manylinux2014 tags unchanged.

Nothing else in the library is architecture-specific: the encoder/decoder and
vgf_dump/vgf_updater tools are generic C++17 with no SIMD intrinsics, and
their CMakeLists.txt files carry no architecture gates.
---
 pip_package/setup.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pip_package/setup.py b/pip_package/setup.py
index 7227ce5..8a94bc9 100644
--- a/pip_package/setup.py
+++ b/pip_package/setup.py
@@ -48,6 +48,8 @@ class BDistWheel(bdist_wheel):
         elif system == "Linux":
             if machine == "aarch64":
                 platformName = "manylinux2014_aarch64"
+            elif machine == "riscv64":
+                platformName = "manylinux_2_39_riscv64"
             else:
                 assert machine == "x86_64"
                 platformName = "manylinux2014_x86_64"
